bench:qa:29.answer_text:
Under Article 28, the notifying authority is the authority that assesses, designates, notifies and monitors notified bodies. In that role, it:
- receives from notified bodies (and can request) all relevant documentation, including providers’ documentation, so it can carry out its assessment/designation/notification/monitoring activities;
- provides the Commission, on request, with all relevant information relating to the notification of a notified body or the maintenance of that body’s competence;
- where a designation is restricted, suspended or withdrawn, takes steps to ensure the notified body’s files are kept and made available to other Member States’ notifying authorities and to market surveillance authorities upon request.

